# Aston Martin DBS V12 coupe, 2007-2012.
#
# The DBS V12: the DB9-based carbon-fibre-bodied flagship with the deeper
# front splitter, the twin vented bonnet, the flared arches, the deeper sills
# and the pronounced rear diffuser. The coupe is modelled; the Volante is a
# different body.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DBS_V12
#
# Dimensions 4.721 x 1.905 m excluding mirrors (2.060 including) x 1.280 m,
# wheelbase 2.740 m. 1.905 m is used, the mirror width excluded.
#
# Shape reference: a DBS V12 coupe in true side elevation, front three-quarter
# and rear three-quarter. The plate 0008 DBS is legible in the front and rear
# views, so the pack is one car. The photographs are monochrome and establish
# shape only, not paint.
#
# Colours: grade (c). Lightning Silver is the 2007 launch colour; Azurite
# Black (2010 UB-2010), Flame Orange and Ceramic Grey (2011-12 Carbon
# Edition) are named special editions. No full UK chart was found. Weights 3,
# 3, 2, 2, total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 307 km/h. Comfort 82/303, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 82. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2007 intro, retires staggered 2035-2038.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-dbs-v12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-dbs-v12.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-dbs-v12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear lens outlines and diffuser shape need
# refinement, and the monochrome photographs do not establish paint. At
# 128 px the low stance, deep sills, vented bonnet and splitter read as a
# DBS V12.


obj=citycar
